From: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] Wait for API limit advisory subscriptions before requests

The finite burst of API requests uses a different connection from the
system-account advisory subscription. Without flushing that subscription
and waiting for route propagation, every advisory can be sent before its
subscriber exists. Flush it and wait for interest on each cluster member
before generating the original 100 requests. Keep the queue limit, domain
and dropped-request assertions unchanged.

Signed-off-by: cl2t <yihong.or@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
--- a/server/jetstream_cluster_4_test.go
+++ b/server/jetstream_cluster_4_test.go
@@ -2986,6 +2986,12 @@
 
 	sub, err := snc.SubscribeSync(JSAdvisoryAPILimitReached)
 	require_NoError(t, err)
+	natsFlush(t, snc)
+	// Requests and advisories use different connections. Wait for interest
+	// on every server before the finite request burst can publish advisories.
+	for _, srv := range c.servers {
+		checkSubInterest(t, srv, srv.SystemAccount().GetName(), JSAdvisoryAPILimitReached, 5*time.Second)
+	}
 
 	// There's a very slim chance that a worker could pick up a request between
 	// pushing to and draining the queue, so make sure we've sent enough of them
